{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1476454-so-what-do-you-think-about-this-new-edition","id":1476454,"title":"So, what do you think about this new edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-15T13:29:10-07:00","id":1476454,"title":"So, what do you think about this new edition?","content":"Well, what the title says<br /> <br /> What do you think about this second edition?<br /> What do you like about it ,what do you dislike about it?<br /> Do you believe the game is better than it's 1st edition iteration?<br /> <br /> What would you want to be diferent?<br /> <br /> I","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T13:35:00-07:00","id":1476455,"title":"","content":"I like it, my current group decided to move our human game into an hunter one, the compacts and conspiracies are very interesting, my group prefer the local type of hunters but I think I will build some backstory for larger tiers too, overall its a very good addition for a pure monster hunting game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T14:03:07-07:00","id":1476460,"title":"","content":"Beyond my normal gripes that apply to 2e in general (ex: Condition bloat, how Professional Training was updated, etc.), I've found 2e to be a completely solid over 1e. For the 2e games, I don't think it's as &quot;interesting&quot; in new designs as some of the other 2e cores got, but by the same token, it's a very clean update that just improves the solid existing formula and didn't have to spend a lot of design time on new systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T14:54:52-07:00","id":1476465,"title":"","content":"I'm generally reluctant to share a lot of my criticism of the books on these forums. Folks here can get heavily invested and very thorough in their readings and rebuttals. I don't mean in any way to hit and run, but I'm probably just going to leave my thoughts here and move on.<br /> <br /> I'm quite disappointed in Hunter Second Edition. I don't think it makes for a bad game book, but I think it hits mediocre at best. Vigil First Edition set a very high bar to meet, and I don't think it had to hit the same mark of writing and design perfectly to be a satisfying and exciting book to get. But in addition to a lot of little things and frustrating decisions that build up in the aggregate, the spirit isn't there.<br /> <br /> Vigil's 1e core had a murky hoariness to it, a sense that the shadows were thick and pretty much anything was waiting out there. As iconic as a lot of the compacts and conspiracies were, they felt like elements in a vast ocean with a lot of room for other things, and much of the information about them that later books rolled out raised more questions than it solved. Apocrypha was rife and contradictory. The first tier was everpresent, and its spirit was present even in higher tiers, with a street-level vantage point concerned with the immediate experience of hunters on the ground. Second Edition feels at once too defined and not focused enough, too invested in details carried over from past books and built on and interconnected, and not enough in what purpose they serve. The first tier feels less present, and the vantage point feels raised, with more attention given to movers and shakers and organizations and connections between defined and listed compacts and conspiracies. It sometimes feels like a Second Edition book written for readers already familiar with First Edition to know not only who these people are but why they should feel invested in them. Less is more, and Second Edition is too &quot;more&quot; and not enough &quot;less.&quot;<br /> <br /> Smaller, more individual points:<br /> <br /> The treatment of Null Mysteriis is more coherent than in First Edition.<br /> The treatment of the Cheiron Group loses its strongest thematic element around which everything else neat and strange about it was wound, that the Field Projects Division was in some sense <i>secondary</i> to a large medical conglomerate, a way of recouping investments in failed experiments. It was most centrally an industry demonstrating the capacity for monstrocity of human society, not through alien invaders but through the simple logic of profit. Cheiron wasn't truly scary and faceless because rumors spread about the ancient lives and many names of the Board of Directors. It was scary and faceless because the corporation wasn't sending you to risk your lives against vampires so that they could see through the devil's eyes, but so that they could catalyze a binding agent that reduces production overhead on medical adhesives by 3%.<br /> The treatment of VASCU just misses the mark completely.<br /> <br /> I like that attention is given to supernatural objects and locations. I don't like that hunters now have a much more distinct Integrity trait from non-hunters, I don't like the way it works, and I especially don't like that despite not working like Integrity works, it is still referred to as Integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T15:55:42-07:00","id":1476467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1476454-so-what-do-you-think-about-this-new-edition?p=1476465#post1476465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm generally reluctant to share a lot of my criticism of the books on these forums. Folks here can get heavily invested and very thorough in their readings and rebuttals. I don't mean in any way to hit and run, but I'm probably just going to leave my thoughts here and move on.<br /> <br /> I'm quite disappointed in Hunter Second Edition. I don't think it makes for a bad game book, but I think it hits mediocre at best. Vigil First Edition set a very high bar to meet, and I don't think it had to hit the same mark of writing and design perfectly to be a satisfying and exciting book to get. But in addition to a lot of little things and frustrating decisions that build up in the aggregate, the spirit isn't there.<br /> <br /> Vigil's 1e core had a murky hoariness to it, a sense that the shadows were thick and pretty much anything was waiting out there. As iconic as a lot of the compacts and conspiracies were, they felt like elements in a vast ocean with a lot of room for other things, and much of the information about them that later books rolled out raised more questions than it solved. Apocrypha was rife and contradictory. The first tier was everpresent, and its spirit was present even in higher tiers, with a street-level vantage point concerned with the immediate experience of hunters on the ground. Second Edition feels at once too defined and not focused enough, too invested in details carried over from past books and built on and interconnected, and not enough in what purpose they serve. The first tier feels less present, and the vantage point feels raised, with more attention given to movers and shakers and organizations and connections between defined and listed compacts and conspiracies. It sometimes feels like a Second Edition book written for readers already familiar with First Edition to know not only who these people are but why they should feel invested in them. Less is more, and Second Edition is too &quot;more&quot; and not enough &quot;less.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>^this, but adding the personal to it:<br /> <br /> Disappointed might not be how I word it, but Second Edition definitely didn't punch as hard as First Edition. Indifferent might be the expression of my feelings.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure I've bitched about this before and else where, but for me the biggest cause of this comes from the way that Chapter 2, where a lot of the feel of Hunter 2nd is established, it a lot more concerned with the world of hunters on an &quot;organizationally&quot; internal basis, where a lot more of the text is interested in the operations hunters within their own structures, how those structures interact with each other, and how it plays out on the chess board arrayed against the night-all of this in contrast where Hunter 1st spent a lot of time both establishing the emotional backdrop and drive of individual hunters and how the sort of nightmares out there form the basis of relationships hunters <i>have</i> with the Vigil. 1st Edition is a lot more streetbound, focused on the individual action and consequences, a lot more casually paranoid. 2nd Edition is more top down and disassociated.<br /> <br /> Another casualty of this is the way that the shadows, grime, and muck of it all don't <i>really</i> feel like they work their way into a hunter's life, attitude, and soul. It's addressed, sure, but because 1st Edition took a more intimate and causal relationship with the acts that make up the Vigil, that version makes it easy to understand how the Vigil warps and eats away at a hunter, how bringing yourself to match the monsters burns away at humanity to keep up in kind. 2nd Edition makes it feel more....professional, even in it's duress. Maybe that works in the age of the hustle and gig economics, but if I really wanted the vibe of the dehumanizing and unrewarding aspect of that sort of stuff expressed in monster hunting, I'd go play #iHunt(and I encourage everyone to go check that out).<br /> <br /> On the whole, Hunter 2nd feels cleaner and more depersonalized than it probably should. I'm still more or less a fan of it, because I'm a fan of 2nd Edition on the whole even as time is showing it's wear and tear, and Hunter 1st is a <i>hard game</i> to one-up because of how well executed 1st edition was, but of the 2nd Editions, it's undoubtedly the one I'm coldest towards. I'd recommend it to keep the gameline up to date with everything else, and that's pretty worth while-but I can't say there's a whole lot that excites me about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-15-2022, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T17:00:10-07:00","id":1476474,"title":"","content":"The &quot;To Be Fair&quot; counter-argument:<br /> <br /> One of the major problems with doing a second edition is that Hunter's Core, much like the Werewolf line on the whole, didn't really leave a whole lot of room to grow or build or do something. It was a really solid core rulebook, and it's a hard thing to follow up on.<br /> <br /> It didn't really have a tone problem or a missing cool kids factor.<br /> It didn't have a muddled focus or direction, a problem of understanding what it is the players do, or why and how and it's larger thematic implications.<br /> It didn't really have a mechanical disassociation from the rest of it's narrative.<br /> And it didn't really have implied spaces that begged for detailing and expansion.<br /> <br /> (If you look at all the other games that made the transition from 1st Edition to 2nd, you can find one or more of the above things that becomes clear with the shift.)<br /> <br /> Hunter was-still is-a hard game to follow up on. About the only thing you could really do more of with the 2nd Edition is lean more into the locality of the Vigil much like how there was a general push to dig into the locality of every other gamelines, getting how specific places with specific histories and supernatural landscapes leads to the particular shapes and forms of hunter responses and organizations (and honestly, some of the ways they did that are very much appreciated, Like SWORN or the Six Stars), and you can only do so much of that before you get 50 flavors of the Union or such. Otherwise, how <i>do </i>you make Hunter 2nd that does something new/expansive while still keeping the game what it is?<br /> <br /> A lot of the answers I have on hand for that are more things that could be served to be baked into a hypothetical 3rd Edition of Chronicles on the whole. For Hunter specifically, most answers I have come out &quot;Do more of what it was doing already&quot; which is not the sort of thing that gets people excited and full of praise the same way they did for their peers. I imagine people who actually had to work on the development of Hunter ran into the same issue, and did the best they could with what they could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-15-2022, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T23:14:44-07:00","id":1476502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1476454-so-what-do-you-think-about-this-new-edition?p=1476467#post1476467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^this, but adding the personal to it:<br /> <br /> Disappointed might not be how I word it, but Second Edition definitely didn't punch as hard as First Edition. Indifferent might be the expression of my feelings.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure I've bitched about this before and else where, but for me the biggest cause of this comes from the way that Chapter 2, where a lot of the feel of Hunter 2nd is established, it a lot more concerned with the world of hunters on an &amp;quot;organizationally&amp;quot; internal basis, where a lot more of the text is interested in the operations hunters within their own structures, how those structures interact with each other, and how it plays out on the chess board arrayed against the night-all of this in contrast where Hunter 1st spent a lot of time both establishing the emotional backdrop and drive of individual hunters and how the sort of nightmares out there form the basis of relationships hunters <i>have</i> with the Vigil. 1st Edition is a lot more streetbound, focused on the individual action and consequences, a lot more casually paranoid. 2nd Edition is more top down and disassociated.<br /> <br /> Another casualty of this is the way that the shadows, grime, and muck of it all don't <i>really</i> feel like they work their way into a hunter's life, attitude, and soul. It's addressed, sure, but because 1st Edition took a more intimate and causal relationship with the acts that make up the Vigil, that version makes it easy to understand how the Vigil warps and eats away at a hunter, how bringing yourself to match the monsters burns away at humanity to keep up in kind. 2nd Edition makes it feel more....professional, even in it's duress. Maybe that works in the age of the hustle and gig economics, but if I really wanted the vibe of the dehumanizing and unrewarding aspect of that sort of stuff expressed in monster hunting, I'd go play #iHunt(and I encourage everyone to go check that out).<br /> <br /> On the whole, Hunter 2nd feels cleaner and more depersonalized than it probably should. I'm still more or less a fan of it, because I'm a fan of 2nd Edition on the whole even as time is showing it's wear and tear, and Hunter 1st is a <i>hard game</i> to one-up because of how well executed 1st edition was, but of the 2nd Editions, it's undoubtedly the one I'm coldest towards. I'd recommend it to keep the gameline up to date with everything else, and that's pretty worth while-but I can't say there's a whole lot that excites me about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a shame because up to this point most 2nd editions had been generally regarded as of the same quality or better than their pedecesors, well i guess some line had to get the short end of the stick","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T23:51:06-07:00","id":1476505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anyoneatall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1476454-so-what-do-you-think-about-this-new-edition?p=1476502#post1476502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a shame because up to this point most 2nd editions had been generally regarded as of the same quality or better than their pedecesors, well i guess some line had to get the short end of the stick</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a little bit unfair of a way to think about it, particularly since the writers and developers gave it a lot of effort. It's more that Hunter is one of the more troublesome first cour First Editions* to adapt, as mentioned because Hunter set a very high bar and little in the apparent to go higher with.<br /> <br /> The tone and mode of attack issues that I and Loserman brought up are definite notes to bring up, and I wouldn't be surprised if a large number of Hunter fans hold it-but for just as many, that's going to work to the betterment of Hunter, particularly as noted with some of the audience vocally present around the time of the Kickstarter. It's by and large a matter of taste-the actual quality is still very much to the expectations of 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> *First edition games made before the CCP dead time, basically Vampire to Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-16-2022, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T01:43:00-07:00","id":1476508,"title":"","content":"A lot of the perceptions of 2e being vast improvements is a lot to do with how much improving some of the cores really needed. The &quot;Big 3&quot; of Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage all had a lot to two in 2e: dump a lot of the hold over stuff from WoD that didn't really serve the CofD, clean up a lot of mechanics, clean up a lot of lore/presentation, and so on. Promethean, Changeling, and Geist had less tonal/thematic issues to address, but benefited from some serious redesigns of core mechanics to better capture what the games are about. Mummy is somewhere between those.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why the biggest debates on the forums around HtV 2e were what to do with Ashwood Abbey... that says something about how much 2e was going to be more of a tweak than a redo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T11:45:14-07:00","id":1476527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1476454-so-what-do-you-think-about-this-new-edition?p=1476508#post1476508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the perceptions of 2e being vast improvements is a lot to do with how much improving some of the cores really needed. The &quot;Big 3&quot; of Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage all had a lot to two in 2e: dump a lot of the hold over stuff from WoD that didn't really serve the CofD, clean up a lot of mechanics, clean up a lot of lore/presentation, and so on. Promethean, Changeling, and Geist had less tonal/thematic issues to address, but benefited from some serious redesigns of core mechanics to better capture what the games are about. Mummy is somewhere between those.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why the biggest debates on the forums around HtV 2e were what to do with Ashwood Abbey... that says something about how much 2e was going to be more of a tweak than a redo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so.<br /> <br /> The other major discussion of the time, around The Code, spoke more towards audience problems rather than Hunter issues. And beyond that, there really wasn't much additional discussion. That doesn't just happen without Hunter being solidly built.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T09:13:41-07:00","id":1490137,"title":"","content":"I don't have any points to make-everything I like less about this edition has already been explained better than I could. But (and this is a purely subjectical view lol) Hunter the Vigil 1e was a masterpiece. It was a really high mark toexpect the same quality of content and they have adressed major issues I had with the game, like The Code being so abstract (for each game I ahve mastered I have had to talk with at least one player about what The Code reallly allows you to do).<br /> <br /> And the treatment of the conspirancies isn't perfect, but if you asked me before getting the book if I preferred having the conspiracies intact or some experimentation I probably would ahve chosen the second one, if anythign because I can mix and match what I like.<br /> <br /> Just a couple of thoughts. Never gonna forgive them for their treatment of AKD tho.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T18:14:33-07:00","id":1491844,"title":"","content":"I am feeling similarly to the rest of the thread: 1e was really, really hard to improve substantially. I\u2019m about to play in my fourth hunter campaign, two successfully concluded, one did not (it fizzled, as happens sometimes).<br /> <br /> All of them are Tier One. My friends and I do not like any of the compacts or conspiracies really, and when we\u2019ve used them, they\u2019re bad guys. Hunter 5e did this apparently (I\u2019ve not read it yet), but that\u2019s neither here nor there for me.<br /> <br /> About the only thing I can\u2019t figure out, and I\u2019ve read the book (skipping a lot of the fluff, I guess) is the new take on Tactics. Do you not buy them anymore with XP? Do you just\u2026agree you know them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9444-joewolz","name":"joewolz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T19:07:46-07:00","id":1491852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>joewolz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1476454-so-what-do-you-think-about-this-new-edition?p=1491844#post1491844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the only thing I can\u2019t figure out, and I\u2019ve read the book (skipping a lot of the fluff, I guess) is the new take on Tactics. Do you not buy them anymore with XP? Do you just\u2026agree you know them?</div> </div> </div> </div>See Step Six of character creation on page 71. Any hunter can perform any Tactic as long as they can risk Willpower for it. Your cell starts out with three favored Tactics that give the primary actor 8-Again, gaining another one every time a member of the cell hits Status 3 in their compact or conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T20:11:38-07:00","id":1491861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1476454-so-what-do-you-think-about-this-new-edition?p=1491852#post1491852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See Step Six of character creation on page 71. Any hunter can perform any Tactic as long as they can risk Willpower for it. Your cell starts out with three favored Tactics that give the primary actor 8-Again, gaining another one every time a member of the cell hits Status 3 in their compact or conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I skipped it somehow. We\u2019re playing tier one with no compacts or conspiracies in play\u2026so we\u2019ll have to figure something else out for getting more I guess","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9444-joewolz","name":"joewolz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T15:52:26-08:00","id":1502781,"title":"","content":"I have a question:<br /> Page 74 of the CoD manual indicates breaking point modifiers are determined by the character's current integrity (+2 for 8-10, +1 for 6-7, etc.).<br /> Page 80+ of HtV would seem to indicate the modifier is instead based on the level of the breaking point, and the modifiers themselves appear to be different; these differences don't appear to be called out as specifically pertaining only to Hunter characters, am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","name":"Burzghash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T16:11:53-08:00","id":1502786,"title":"","content":"The Integrity trait that hunters use in 2e (the one in the HTV book), despite its name, is very different from the Integrity trait non-hunters use (the one in the CofD rulebook). A character uses one or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}